+  // ---- Raw stack pushes/pops --------------------------------------------
+  //
+  // The JIT's stack discipline moves the stack pointer one 8-byte slot at a
+  // time. IA-64 hardware only requires natural alignment for each access, so an
+  // 8-byte-aligned sp is fine inside JIT code; the 16-byte ABI alignment is
+  // re-established at ABI call boundaries by setupUnalignedABICall().
